          "heading": "Safety and scientific integrity",
          "content": "Actual heat treatment involves hot furnaces, liquid-metal hazards, quench fires, boiling liquids, thermal shock, fumes, and sometimes toxic alloying elements. Calculators here intentionally lack material-specific design allowables, chemical hazard details and certified treatment schedules. Do not construct a laboratory process from the sample constants. Instructors should substitute vetted equipment procedures, conduct institution-specific risk assessments, and use approved safety supervision. Physics mechanisms in this manuscript are standard teaching abstractions, while invented numerical constants illustrate algebra only. The appendix explains how to audit a model, independently verify structural claims and report uncertainty before presenting a conclusion.\n\n\n\n**Guiding question:** Which phases can lower free energy, and why may equilibrium be delayed?",
